    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">When two binary numbers are added, a carry may be produced out of a bit position.<br>You are given two binary numbers of equal length.<br>For each bit position, determine whether a carry is produced OUT of that position (taking into account the carry coming in from the position to its right).<br>Print a binary string of the same length, from the most significant position to the least significant, with <const>1</const> where a carry is produced and <const>0</const> otherwise.<br>The rightmost position has no incoming carry.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> A binary string <var>A</var>.<br><strong>Line 2:</strong> A binary string <var>B</var> of the same length.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> A binary string of the same length, marking each position where a carry is produced out.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &le; length of <var>A</var>, length of <var>B</var> &le; 10<br><var>A</var> and <var>B</var> contain only <const>0</const> and <const>1</const></div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">0010\n1111</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            